{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Is it not this one in which he divines?</b> It means he tested you by it, to know whether you are thieves, like \"I divined\" (Genesis 30:27), and likewise \"for he will certainly divine\" (Genesis 44:15); and its meaning is, why did you not fear, for to test you I placed the silver goblet before you and closed my eyes until you took it. And Rabbi Yonah said that the meaning of \"in it\" is \"on its account,\" and so its meaning is: he will ask diviners on its account, and \"for he will certainly divine,\" for a man like me has diviners. And some say that the goblet was engraved, and through it he would look at his brothers and say, this one is the firstborn and this one was born after him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {0 "Resolved ר' יונה to Rabbi Yonah; resolved וי\"א to 'and some say.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:00.208125725Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}